# 🚀 Cloudflare Worker Search Tracker - Deployment Guide

## Overview

This system provides a **hybrid search tracking solution** that combines:
- ✅ **Instant local storage** (works offline, privacy-friendly)
- ✅ **Cloud sync via Cloudflare Workers** (cross-device, persistent)
- ✅ **Global aggregated analytics** (everyone's searches combined)

---

## 📁 Project Structure

After setup, your project should look like this:

```
alfredmayaki.github.io/
├── wrangler.toml              ← Worker configuration
├── search-tracker.js          ← Worker code (API endpoints)
├── search-tracker-api.js      ← Frontend API client
├── index.html                 ← Homepage with search
├── tagcloud.html              ← Tag cloud visualization
├── CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOYMENT.md   ← This guide
└── ... (other files)
```

**All worker files are in the root directory** - this is the standard Cloudflare Workers convention.

